WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.730
Hi, and welcome to the course.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.470
This course will be the first of series'
of courses where you will learn to build

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.750
great products.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.530
&gt;&gt; We thought a lot about whether
entrepreneurship can be taught.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.140
And there are many courses and
reference materials out there.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.190
But we wondered whether that material,
or

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:18.700
series of courses could really
transform someone into an entrepreneur.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.612
Someone that is an unconventional
hacker, a risk taker, and

00:00:21.612 --> 00:00:23.310
a jack of all trades.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.660
&gt;&gt; Successful entrepreneurship is
a lot more than the inner workings of

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.420
a company, or
the character of the founders.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.530
It involves a number of external factors
which make it extremely difficult

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.850
to have a single formula for success.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.630
Every moment in history
will only happen once.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.200
There would be only one Airbnb.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.830
There wouldn't be any other Google.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:46.410
Fortunately, there are plenty of
other problems left for you to solve.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.910
&gt;&gt; Yeah, and this course is designed
to teach you some practices and

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.460
processes that Silicon Valley
companies have developed

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.160
over the past few years on how to create
beautiful and meaningful products.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.950
We hope you can use them
as our framework to build

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.570
a business of your own.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:02.250
&gt;&gt; Because start ups are risky and
costly business,

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.450
it is always wise to validate early on,
build only what you need, and not more.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.790
And iterate as fast as you can.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.620
Throughout this course we'll
talk to several start-ups

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.050
who have done just that.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:14.940
Let's hear from them now.

